    "grading": "Correctness as above, per arm and per tip cell (TRUE n=18, FALSE n=18). Visits are reported per cell: a TRUE tip should be worth one visit to any policy that uses it; a FALSE tip measures how much a policy pays for trusting it. Uniform prior otherwise, so the only efficiency statement is the paired per-cell comparison, never an overall one.",
